            <ArticleTitle>Experimental evaluation in man of analgesic effects.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1616-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A device operated by compression has been studied in order to define a method of measuring analgesic effects. Three analgesics (metamizol, acetylsalicylic acid and ketobemidone) and placebo have been tested in man to verify the adequacy of this apparatus and its sensitivity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
